  "CAKE": "retention flat at ~1.0 through N=400 (each fact -> separate memory slot, zero weight change, no inter-edit interference). Locality degrades gently (1.0->0.55 at N=400) because a larger populated memory has more chances for a control prompt to exceed the fixed gate 0.45. 400 edits written in 1.8 s, 0 gradient steps.",
  "ROME": "sequential single-layer edits catastrophically interfere: locality collapses 0.85->0.00 by N=50 (model destroyed). Retention reads 0.0 from N=1 due to a fresh-pass scoring artifact after keep_original_weight=False (documented earlier in project); the ROBUST, unambiguous signal is the locality collapse. 100 edits took 758 s.",
